{"title": "Christmas tree fire: watered vs. a dry tree.", "description": "Many of us enjoy the fresh and natural qualities of a live Christmas tree. But too often we get carried away in the holiday rush and forget to water. Christmas trees need to be watered daily to not only keep them green and living but more importantly not to allow them to become overly dry. Overly dry trees are a major, fast burning fire hazard in your home. \n\nNational Institute of Standards and Technology has shown us just how quickly a dry tree burns and starts a fire that could soon engulf your home, versus a well-hydrated tree that burns at a slower and less rapid rate.\n\nWater your trees so that the only lights you see at Christmas are the lights on your tree and home, not the lights of the Midland Fire Department.", "uploader": "City of Midland, Texas - City Government", "uploader_id": "100064423074760", "thumbnail": "https://scontent-ord5-1.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t15.5256-10/24521589_10155327478398178_640172773913657344_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_tt6&cstp=mx1280x670&ctp=s960x960&_nc_cat=106&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=50ce42&_nc_ohc=lhxebkXutpsQ7kNvwH6g6Ga&_nc_oc=Adris3G5nAhtZXLuREO5Y3qqISy3WrAqgsHfoFzsax5WN9PmTWfXALnrKEE7nG4AhEI&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent-ord5-1.xx&_nc_gid=ddVSPdj2GeGn0-arw4ew-w&_nc_ss=70289&oh=00_AQT3Y47Mlqwe8wftj6dU40CvEgnjrknTjHBSSvfIvkm_5A&oe=6AF068CF", "view_count": 1578, "concurrent_view_count": 0, "duration": 137.156, "id": "10155327468498178", "formats": [{"format_id": "sd", "quality": -3, "url": "https://video-ord5-2.xx.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m412/AQP44KatrYhin1_daXxSRdrNydLsIySIPMwWKdnNc_ravqrAm3wceRYCg2p1nWSwKtyDpioyrFkMtkieRCq1tAdz.mp4?_nc_cat=110&_nc_sid=8bf8fe&_nc_ht=video-ord5-2.xx.fbcdn.net&_nc_ohc=lkkxrnXV92UQ7kNvwGE6hw2&efg=eyJ2ZW5jb2RlX3RhZyI6Inhwdl9wcm9ncmVzc2l2ZS5GQUNFQk9PSy4uQzMuNDAwLnN2ZV9zZCIsInhwdl9hc3NldF9pZCI6NDE0MDkyODYxNTM1MDg0LCJhc3NldF9hZ2VfZGF5cyI6MzI0MCwidmlfdXNlY2FzZV9pZCI6MTAxMjIsImR1cmF0aW9uX3MiOjEzNywidXJsZ2VuX3NvdXJjZSI6Ind3dyJ9&ccb=17-1&_nc_gid=ddVSPdj2GeGn0-a